# broker#21 - installed as /etc/default/earlyoom.
#
# VSCode Server and Claude Code run in init.scope, outside any slice systemd can
# cap, so a per-process killer is the containment that reaches them.
#
#   -r 3600   one memory report an hour in the journal (the package default)
#   -m 10     SIGTERM below 10% available (~790 MiB at 8 GB), SIGKILL below 5%.
#             There is no swap, so earlyoom's swap condition always holds and
#             memory alone decides.
#   --avoid   the bus and the way in: redis-server, tailscaled, systemd*,
#             dbus-daemon, and exe.dev's own exe-init and sshd. Only -300, not
#             an exclusion: dev tooling inherits exe.dev's oom_score_adj -1000,
#             so the bus also needs the drop-ins' OOMScoreAdjust=-900 to rank
#             below it
#   --prefer  dev tooling: node, npx (titled `npm exec <pkg>`), and VSCode
#             Server's node processes, whose comm is MainThread
#
# No -p: it needs CAP_SYS_NICE, which this DynamicUser unit does not have.
#
# Regexes are UNQUOTED and space-free. The unit runs `earlyoom $EARLYOOM_ARGS`,
# and systemd splits that on whitespace without interpreting quotes - the
# package's own quoted --avoid example would arrive with literal quotes and
# never match. tests/deploy/test_memory_protection.py pins both lists.
EARLYOOM_ARGS="-r 3600 -m 10 --avoid ^(redis-server|tailscaled|systemd.*|dbus-daemon|exe-init|sshd)$ --prefer ^(node|npm.*|npx|MainThread)$"
